    {
      "id": "bs-001",
      "name": "Build Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "notes": "Counts total / valid / invalid for the run and returns those numbers to the form.",
      "position": [
        1420,
        440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\nconst total = items.length;\nconst valid = items.filter(i => String(i.json.status || '').toLowerCase() === 'valid').length;\nconst invalid = total - valid;\nreturn [{ json: { total, valid, invalid, date: DateTime.now().toFormat('LLLL d, yyyy') } }];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-main",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1080,
        -96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FEEA87",
        "width": 540,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## ✉️ Email Verification — Searchbug (api_emver)\n\nVerify a single email address or a whole CSV of them, save every result to Google Sheets, and get a total / valid / invalid count for the run — all from one web form.\n\n### How it works\n1. Enter ONE email, OR leave it blank and upload a CSV (with an \"email\" column).\n2. Single or Bulk? routes the input; both paths merge at Normalize.\n3. The workflow verifies each email with Searchbug's Email Verification API.\n4. Each result is saved to Google Sheets, then Build Summary returns the run totals (total / valid / invalid) back to the form.\n\n### How to set up\n- [ ] Add your Searchbug CO_CODE + PASS in the Verify Email node (Query Parameters)\n- [ ] Connect your OWN Google Sheets account in the Save node\n- [ ] Change the Document to your own spreadsheet + tab\n- [ ] Activate and share the form link\n\n### Columns saved\nemail, status, sub_status, free_email, catchall_domain, did_you_mean, domain, mx_found, smtp_provider, date_checked\n\n### Customization\n- CSV works with or without a header row.\n- Filter the results in Sheets by status to get just the invalid addresses."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -480,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## 1. Enter Email or Upload CSV\n\nSingle or Bulk? checks whether the Email field was filled. Single email → Set Single Email; CSV upload → Extract CSV. Both paths merge at Normalize into one consistent `email` field."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## 2. Verify & Extract\n\nVerify Email calls the Searchbug Email Verification API for each address (continues on error). Extract Result flattens the response into clean columns."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1060,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FCD9DD",
        "width": 260,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## ⚠️ 3. Save to Google Sheets\n\nConnect your OWN Google Sheets credential and select your spreadsheet and tab. Create your tab with headers matching the 10 columns in this node.\n\nDon't click ⋮ → Refresh — it erases the column mapping."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-4",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1360,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## 4. Run Summary\n\nBuild Summary counts total / valid / invalid for the run and returns those numbers to the form, so you see the result right after submitting.\n\nEverything is already saved in Google Sheets by this point — this node only reports on it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
